  "id": "Compound::DB00277 - Gene::1558",
  "verbalization": "Theophylline is implicated in the regulation of Cyp2c8 through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Theophylline to Cyp2c9, which is involved in oxidoreductase activity, and Cyp2c8 is a participant in this activity. The second pathway connects Theophylline to Cyp2e1, which is involved in arachidonic acid monooxygenase activity, and again Cyp2c8 is a participant in this process. These two pathways suggest that Theophylline may influence Cyp2c8 through different enzymatic mechanisms, both involving oxidative processes. The shared involvement of Cyp2c8 in these distinct metabolic pathways indicates a potential functional overlap, though the exact mechanism by which Theophylline affects Cyp2c8 remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Cyp2c8 in oxidative metabolism, with Theophylline potentially modulating its activity through interactions with different substrates.",
